{"name":"Saltbox","hex":"#f5e9d9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"saltbox","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A box for keeping salt in.","A similar box formerly used as a percussion instrument in burlesque music."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saltbox"}],"entries":[{"title":"Saltbox (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Saltbox is the fourth full-length album by the Red Aunts. It was released in 1996 on Epitaph."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/94/Red_Aunts_Saltbox.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saltbox_(album)","wikidata":"Q7406044"},{"title":"Saltbox house","blocks":[{"text":"A saltbox house is a gable-roofed residential structure that is typically two stories in the front and one in the rear, so that the front roof is considerably shorter than the back one. It is a traditional New England-style of home, originally timber-framed, which takes its name from its resemblance to a type of slant-topped lidded wooden box in which salt was once kept."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Thomas_Lee_House%2C_East_Lyme_%28New_London_County%2C_Connecticut%29.jpg/330px-Thomas_Lee_House%2C_East_Lyme_%28New_London_County%2C_Connecticut%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saltbox_house","wikidata":"Q7080212"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Nehemiah_Royce_House%2C_Wallingford%2C_Connecticut.JPG/500px-Nehemiah_Royce_House%2C_Wallingford%2C_Connecticut.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Nehemiah_Royce_House%2C_Wallingford%2C_Connecticut.JPG/1280px-Nehemiah_Royce_House%2C_Wallingford%2C_Connecticut.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","s